WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.190
Haiti is a collapsing state.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.649
We are talking about the poorest nation in
the so-called West, whose inhabitants are

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:10.980
in one of the most bleak and depressing situations
of misery in the world.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.670
Haiti is the scene of a tragedy that has been
going on for centuries, which the international

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.100
community does not seem willing, nor able,
to remedy.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.460
The blame for such a disaster lies not only
with the uncontrollable forces of nature,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.590
but also with the great powers, France and
the United States above all, as well as the

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.750
rulers of Haiti themselves, corrupt to the
core.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:38.210
We are talking about a state where it is common
to eat Mud Cakes, real "mud cakes mixed with

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:44.700
powder and food grease, a popular option in
Cité Soleil, one of the poorest slums in

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.050
Port-au-Prince, the capital, where hunger
is a daily problem.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:53.360
Port au prince has now fallen into the hands
of gangs, and has turned into a kind of no-man's

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.360
land.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.790
But, what are they, the origins of such chaos?

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:06.400
Is it possible to trace them?

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:13.390
The story of Haiti is perhaps one of the most
distressing and difficult to tell.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:18.390
Once called the Jewel of the Antilles, the
Island of Hispaniola, now divided between

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.820
Haiti, to the west, and the Dominican Republic,
to the east, was the richest colony in the

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.820
entire New World.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.570
The ancient Taino people, composed of "amiable,
tractable, peaceful, Indians," as Christopher

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:34.510
Columbus had described them in his letters,
were quickly decimated by the conquistadores

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.210
by sword and disease.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:41.659
The sudden disappearance of the locals, however,
prompted European settlers to quickly look

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:46.900
for another source of labor to exploit in
the cultivation of Hispaniola's main resource:

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:47.900
sugar.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.850
The colonists opted to recruit as many slaves
as possible, turning their sights, naturally,

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.320
to West Africa, and finding a solution in
the infamous Atlantic Route.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:03.970
In the span of 30 years, from 1517 to 1540,
more than 30,000 Africans were, pardon the

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:08.950
term, imported to Hispaniola, and, shortly
thereafter, the western part of the island,

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:14.090
still sparsely frequented by the Spanish,
gradually became a haunt for buccaneers committing

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.160
raids in the Caribbean Sea, many of them French.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:22.560
Frenchmen who, in the mid-17th century, finally
succeeded in establishing themselves in the

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.440
western quadrant of the island, obviously
in an entirely illegitimate form, naming it

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.660
"Saint-Domingue."

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.660
Haiti alone came to account for as much as
50 percent of the entire French Gross National

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:39.280
Product, exporting to the Old Continent not
only sugar, but also coffee, cocoa, tobacco,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.750
cotton, indigo and several other products
considered exotic.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:48.989
It is by no means a coincidence that Saint-Domingue
was, at that time, the richest colony on the

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:52.829
globe and the most active mercantile center
in the New World, whose productive.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:58.519
The entire Haitian society was compressed
by rigid social castes in the 18th century.

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:04.830
At the top were the "great whites," the landowners,
the colonial elite patched up with Metropolitan

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.309
French, which amounted to about 40,000 individuals.

00:03:07.309 --> 00:03:13.000
The second social class was the mulattos,
born of unions, in most cases violent, between

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.209
whites and slaves, which consisted of just
28,000 people.

00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:23.220
Finally, there were the 450,000 slaves, who
led a life of deprivation, hunger and pain.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.890
"This slave colony," observed the Marquis
du Rouvray in the late eighteenth century,

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:33.659
"is like a city ready to be attacked: we are
walking on barrels loaded with gunpowder."

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:38.660
Well, blowing up those barrels, in 1789, came
the French Revolution.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:44.280
Inspired by the ideals that had shocked Paris,
and tired of the summary massacres carried

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.010
out by the whites, mestizos and freed slaves,
under the leadership of the now free man Toussaint

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:54.890
Louverture and the fugitive Jean Jacques Dessalines,
responded to violence with violence.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:59.860
I have given the French cannibals blood for
blood," proclaimed Dessalines, considered

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:05.860
the father of the Haitian nation and nicknamed
the Black Napoleon, "I have avenged America",

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.900
he said.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:12.310
The new republic thus became the first independent
nation in all of Latin America, the second

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:16.380
on the entire continent, anticipated only
by the United States.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:21.580
In no other case throughout history has an
enslaved people been able to break the chains

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.030
of servitude and defeat, with a military response.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.740
Finally, the name Saint-Domingue was changed,
in fact, to Haiti.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:34.729
Emerging out of the chaos, however, was - once
again - the ruling power elite, the 3 percent

00:04:34.729 --> 00:04:39.930
of the population that had enjoyed greater
benefits and freedoms under the former colonizers,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.780
and which reintroduced the typical slave system.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.950
In other words, the French colonial legacy
was perpetuated by a simple handover.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.880
What is more, Haitians, although free, found
themselves living in a world completely hostile

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.009
to the idea of a territory self-governed by
blacks.

00:04:56.009 --> 00:05:01.580
An independent Haiti was in fact a nightmare
for all those powers for whom slavery was

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.240
kinda normal, starting with the United States.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.600
The so called "international community" or
rather Europe, condemned the Haitian model,

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:19.090
that of a nation of freed slaves, Europeans
and the United States coordinated to prepare

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.580
a full-fledged diplomatic embargo on the island.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:27.720
France refused to recognize Haiti’s existence
as a state, and intimated that it was necessary

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.760
to pay compensation due to land confiscation
after the revolution.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.480
It's an absurdity, since it is usually the
losers who have to pay compensation, if you

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.480
think about that.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.880
The request was formalized, so to speak, in
1825, when a French ship loaded with cannons

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.160
entered Port-au-Prince, and an emissary of
King Charles X intimated to the Haitians that

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:56.380
they must pay a debt of 150 million francs
to be paid in five annual installments.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:00.289
To repay the debt Haiti sought a loan from
a group of...French banks.

00:06:00.289 --> 00:06:01.380
That’s it.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:07.180
In this way, the island's economy sank, and
the state coffers were depleted for generations

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.180
to come.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:13.060
The impossibility of having an economically
sound nation was fertile ground for coups

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.930
and government assassinations.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:21.620
Indeed, since 1855, the average office of
Haitian presidents has amounted to just one

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.620
year.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.270
There is no question that being president
of Haiti should not be a pleasant job: we

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:31.660
can be reminded of this by the last head of
state in chronological order, Jovenel Moise,

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:36.770
who was killed in 2021 in his presidential
residence by an unidentified gang group.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.870
As if that weren't enough, the U.S. also got
in the way.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.730
As early as the beginning of the twentieth
century, the United States had practically

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:48.120
taken possession of the Dominican Republic,
the eastern half of Hispaniola, which in the

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.030
previous course had repeatedly gained independence
from Spain.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:57.949
Then, in 1915, Woodrow Wilson gave orders
to initiate the invasion of Haiti as well,

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:00.319
in order to "help" the people.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:05.360
The interrupted French imperialism, then,
changed only in the origin of the master.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.590
Haiti was seen as an insult to imperialism,
and the United States, which feared the German

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:15.800
investments begun in the late 19th century
in the island, applied so called the Monroe

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.500
Doctrine, idealistically summarized as "America
to Americans," to the letter.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.780
More pragmatically, Wilson sought a military
base in the Caribbean Sea.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:29.630
The marines took control of Haiti's tax revenues
and the national bank, forcing the passage

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:36.229
of a new constitution that in essence nullified
the ban, established in 1804, that prevented

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:39.570
any foreigner from owning land in the country.

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:45.000
Without a blow, in short, Washington had created
a new vassal state that would remain loyal

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.480
even after the occupation ended in 1934.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.620
The occupation of the Dominican Republic,
however, had ended in 1924, but after six

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.599
years of peace, the United States unleashed
the coup that brought Rafael Leonidas Trujillo

00:07:59.599 --> 00:08:03.659
to power.

00:08:03.659 --> 00:08:13.690
Under Trujillo, nationalist thinking was institutionalized
and this traced the origins of the Dominican

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:20.150
people back to the conquistadores, they mixed
it with anti-Haitian sentiment, when in 1937,

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:24.409
Trujillo had tens of thousands of Haitians
residing in the territory of the Dominican

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:29.110
Republic killed with a method that was peculiar,
simple and cruel.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:33.659
In fact, we refer to the entire operation
as the "parsley massacre".

00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:37.779
Upon meeting the people, the military would
ask them what it was all about: anyone who

00:08:37.779 --> 00:08:43.120
failed to correctly pronounce the word perejil,
meaning parsley, in Spanish, reciting the

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.900
word with a mousy "r"...

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:50.680
Actually in English I just found out that
the typical "R" French people say when speaking,

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.580
is actually called "French R"...

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.320
Not ehm, what did I say?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.560
"Mousy R" [???]

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:02.800
... would automatically be considered Francophone,
hence Haitian and subject to physical elimination.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:08.780
You should know, that since 1915, but especially
from 1946 onward, the United States, through

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:15.080
various economic and humanitarian aid packages,
has wisely played a key role in Haitian politics.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.930
Great, the population is safe.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:23.019
Yes, In an earthly reality like ours, these
subsidies simply went into the wrong pockets,

00:09:23.019 --> 00:09:24.750
those of the Haitian rulers.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:30.140
The most rapacious to take advantage of so-called
Western benevolence was an intellectual at

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:36.120
first very well-liked by many: physician Francois
Duvalier, nicknamed "Papa Doc."

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.209
Duvalier was elected president in 1957.

00:09:38.209 --> 00:09:42.329
However, it took little to turn him into a
dictator.

00:09:42.329 --> 00:09:47.910
First, Papa Doc organized a personal vigilante
force, These death squads came to be nicknamed

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.690
"Tonton Macoutes," an appellation that, according
to Haitian folklore, was attributed to the

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:56.779
boogeyman who, at night, would kidnap children
by hiding them in a sack.

00:09:56.779 --> 00:10:01.970
It is difficult to say how many people disappeared
at the hands of Duvalier's teams, but the

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:07.490
estimates are not the most comforting: there
is talk of tens of thousands of desaparecidos.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:11.769
Basically if you had any doubt about Duvalier,
this could lead you to a mass grave along

00:10:11.769 --> 00:10:13.030
with your entire family.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:18.529
Nevertheless, the international community
did not pay much attention to Papa Doc's schizophrenic

00:10:18.529 --> 00:10:19.529
behavior.

00:10:19.529 --> 00:10:24.540
Indeed, during his first four - and bloodiest
- years in power, Duvalier received from Washington

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.250
the beauty of more than $40 million, most
of it in the form of outright gifts.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:35.830
The White House, as reported in Paul Farmer's
essay The Uses of Haiti, had only one purpose:

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:37.779
"to keep Duvalier in Power."

00:10:37.779 --> 00:10:43.110
It was necessary to prevent Haiti from going
the way of socialist Cuba and continuing to

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.850
serve the interests of the U.S. government,
despite the fact that, beginning in the 1960s,

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.889
thousands of Haitians preferred to flee on
makeshift boats to the coast of Florida in

00:10:53.889 --> 00:10:57.579
search of political asylum rather than remain
on the island.

00:10:57.579 --> 00:11:02.889
Corruption, after all, was so entrenched as
to be an accepted practice throughout Haiti,

00:11:02.889 --> 00:11:08.180
even today senior government officials exploit
their position to amass power and wealth at

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:14.700
the expense of ordinary citizens, and police
smuggle fuel, of which there is a shortage,

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.790
to sell on the black market.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:21.810
On closer inspection, even the imposition
of the official language, French, testifies

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:27.420
to the imbalances that snake through a nation
incapable of coming to terms with the past.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:30.470
In fact, all state business is conducted in
French.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:34.970
However, only 10 percent of the inhabitants
are able to express themselves in this language,

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.250
and less than 5 percent speak it fluently.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.209
Indeed, the idiom of the masses is Haitian
Creole.

00:11:40.209 --> 00:11:45.600
The problem is that to be successful in Haiti
you necessarily have to speak French.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.450
One result of this language oppression is
the abominable national illiteracy rate, which

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.930
approaches 90 percent in the cities and is
even higher in rural areas.

00:11:54.930 --> 00:12:00.330
The reason is that people are needed, manpower
in the fields, for all those families who

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:05.240
cannot get by, partly because the search for
work has driven almost all Haitians to the

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.240
capital.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:12.079
This demographic imbalance, whereby the inhabitants
of the entire country total 11 million - in

00:12:12.079 --> 00:12:18.490
a territory that is as vast as Tuscany in
Italy - is a burden to a long-standing problem

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:24.269
on the island: the continuing destruction
of ecosystems and soil erosion.

00:12:24.269 --> 00:12:29.770
Try taking a look at satellite images nearby
Haiti's border with the Dominican Republic.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:34.639
You will notice how, on the left, the vegetation
appears to be much less prominent.

00:12:34.639 --> 00:12:35.639
What does this mean?

00:12:35.639 --> 00:12:41.160
It means that Haiti is a predominantly mountainous
country, and over the past 200 years the inhabitants

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.230
have been indiscriminately cutting down trees
without replanting them.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:50.149
The spectacle that unfolds every single year
during the five months of uninterrupted rainfalls,

00:12:50.149 --> 00:12:54.530
when rivers of mud slide down the mountain
slopes, is just one of the visible effects

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.870
of this savage deforestation.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:02.260
The main reason for Haitians to destroy their
land is the scarcity of fuel, with wood having

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:07.890
been the only material for lighting a fire
for centuries: people can afford to cook exclusively

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:11.470
with charcoal, which requires large quantities
of wood.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:16.570
And here, we come to yet another hoax for
the Haitian people: most of the best land

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:21.280
domestically produces crops for export, NOT
for the domestic market.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:26.610
Haiti, which would be an agricultural country,
is nothing more than a net importer of food.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:31.529
If you are wondering why, suffice it to say
that almost all of the land is controlled

00:13:31.529 --> 00:13:35.269
by the 3% that represents the Haitian elite.

00:13:35.269 --> 00:13:40.110
Of course, the money that flows into the pockets
of the local oligarchy through exports is

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:44.730
not redistributed into the national economy,
to build, I don't know, roads or hospitals,

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:49.730
but is spent in foreign markets: the United
States, Europe and the Gulf countries.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:55.740
And so, while a sugarcane cutter can call
himself lucky if he earns $1 a day, the domestic

00:13:55.740 --> 00:14:01.089
and foreign companies -let's be explicit for
the sake of fairness, U.S.companies that manage

00:14:01.089 --> 00:14:03.610
the land, make stellar profits..

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:08.750
Faced with a condition of permanent exploitation,
one should therefore not be surprised that

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:14.720
so many Haitians have joined organized crime
and gangs, which are the same as Papa Doc's

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.079
Ton ton macoutes.

00:14:17.079 --> 00:14:23.029
Continuing to surf the waves of Haitian history,
we come to 1990, the year when the pro-democracy

00:14:23.029 --> 00:14:27.870
Presbyterian Jean-Bertrand Aristide incredibly,
given his predecessors-won the presidential

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:30.790
election with 67 percent of the vote.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:35.850
This was an incredible result, considering
the history of Haiti.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.079
But what happened?

00:14:37.079 --> 00:14:43.980
Well, the Americans come again, forced Aristide
into exile, imposed a dictator, the UN declared

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.910
an embargo on Haiti, and after four years
Bill Clinton came back to fix the disaster

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:51.540
that the United States itself had committed.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:56.600
Aristide came back, was deposed, came back
again, was accused of corruption, and in 2004

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.490
a good civil war broke out.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:03.510
Or at least, that was how the UN justified
the deployment of MINUSTAH forces, that is

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:08.240
the United Nations Stabilization Mission in
Haiti, which was supposed to lead the country

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.990
through a democratic transition.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:15.070
And if you think you have already seen hell,
know that until now we have solely visited

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.070
purgatory.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:18.620
Haiti, in fact, has been the scene, over the
past two decades, of natural disasters that

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:24.620
have destroyed not only its society but also
any tiny chance of getting back on its feet.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:30.259
As mentioned above, gangs have very clear
intentions: to take control of the black market

00:15:30.259 --> 00:15:34.160
and manage the drug trade, but without assuming
power.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.190
Even should one gang be able to undermine
the others, attempting a coup would be very

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:44.399
counterproductive: Haiti is already in the
hands of criminal gangs, and going to government

00:15:44.399 --> 00:15:48.670
would only mean losing the trust of those
who support them and see them as the only

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.870
solution to the current political disaster.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:56.250
This is well known by one of Port-au-Prince's
most powerful leaders, Jimmy Chérizier, whose

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:59.790
nickname, by the way, is "Barbecue" ...and
I'll let you imagine why.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.750
In short, here we are, peering through the
gates of Hell.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:08.829
I confess to you that in the face of so much
anguish, I have no solution, no moral to say

00:16:08.829 --> 00:16:09.959
at the end of this video.

00:16:09.959 --> 00:16:14.980
And yet, I feel so much frustrated with an
international community that, in concrete

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:19.060
terms, does nothing at all, except to make
promises and promises...

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:25.060
In October 2022, for example, Henry requested
the deployment of foreign military forces

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:29.589
in Port-au-Prince, with the aim of quelling
the violent gang clash that had broken out

00:16:29.589 --> 00:16:31.350
the previous July in Cité Soleil.

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.319
Do you know who answered the call?

00:16:33.319 --> 00:16:34.870
Yep, the United States.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:40.220
A tragicomic outcome for the situation of
a nation, Haiti, that can neither rid itself

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:46.610
of its past nor extricate itself from the
evils that perennially afflict it and that,

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:52.110
unfortunately, fall on the eleven and a half
million Haitians who, every single day, see

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.540
their hopes fade more and more.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.430
In Haiti, the stars do not shine.

